  "name": "Khuli Chana",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Mmabatho in 1982, Khuli Chana rose to prominence as a central figure in the Motswako movement, a hip-hop style defined by its blend of English and Setswana. He initially gained recognition as a member of the rap group Morafe before embarking on a solo career that yielded the acclaimed album Motswakoriginator. His work frequently centers on this specific Mahikeng-born cultural sound. In 2013, he survived a high-profile incident involving the South African police, which led to a legal settlement. Beyond his studio output, he has functioned as an ambassador for brands like Absolut and performed as an opening act for international artists, including Drake.",
